From 68a8845d51d4a00f7ee80bba63352731352f08a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forklift <forklift@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:05:26 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] forklift: S1, redundant keyframes kept only temporarily

With FORKLIFT_SLAM_S1 on, each processed keyframe is judged after it is in the graph and linked,
before loop closing: the nearest live permanent node within 0.3 m and 0.35 rad of its corrected
pose (a nearer temporary or misaligned node does not hide it); if the new scan matches that node's
chain with at least link_match_minimum_response_fine it is temporary, otherwise permanent. The
chain is the running scans when the node is among them (the sequential match's own response, no
extra match), otherwise the node and its live id neighbours within link_scan_maximum_distance of
the new scan (one more sequential match, timed as s1_match). Temporary nodes are never loop
candidates. After each keyframe the temporary nodes born at least FORKLIFT_SLAM_S1_BUFFER (B)
keyframes ago are deleted in id order through the deletion contract, except running, last and new
scans; one whose neighbours would not stay connected without it is promoted to permanent and
recorded. The marks live outside the Mapper. The S1 refusal of 0002 is lifted. The trace gains
set_value and the S1 counts. gtests: the near permanent node, due nodes, the disconnect check.
